                        "name": "How To Plant And Grow Vinca - Hunker",
                        "url": "https://www.hunker.com/13404331/when-to-plant-vinca/",
                        "datePublished": "2021-11-04T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Nov 4, 2021",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.hunker.com/13404331",
                        "snippet": "Vincas are fans of acidic soil, and their ideal soil pH level is around 5.5. Vincas survive droughts well but don't like wet soil, so give them a home in loamy or sandy soil that drains well. Space your plants 10 to 12 inches apart to promote airflow and minimize the risk of fungus. Mulch the plants lightly if desired.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-03T21:33:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Annual+Vinca+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4505974877126879&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=RX6tTDSAfRoBFNAV6R-FHu1AV2LQnTHC",
