                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardenersworld.com/how-to/grow-plants/bacopa-plant",
                        "snippet": "How to propagate bacopa. The easiest way to make more bacopa plants is by taking stem cuttings between March and August. Cut a shoot around 10-15cm long. Trim the cutting at the bottom, just below a leaf joint and remove the leaves from the bottom half. Insert the cutting into a pot of compost and wait for it to root.",
