                        "thumbnailUrl": "https://www.bing.com/th?id=OIP.40oRnHnYrj8z4RjktaP4DwHaFC&w=80&h=80&c=1&pid=5.1",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.medicinenet.com/what_is_bacopa_good_for_and_are_there_side_effects/article.htm",
                        "snippet": "Bacopa is safe to take for up to 12 weeks, and severe side effects are rare. In these rare cases, bacopa may: Upset digestion. The most common side effect of bacopa supplements is digestive problems. Bacopa can cause nausea, diarrhea, upset stomach, and fatigue.. It might also slow your gut transit time: i.e., how long it takes for food and waste to move through your gut.",
