                        "snippet": "Balloon flower gets its common name from the unopened flower buds which resemble hot air balloons. Children love to grow this plant for the balloon-like buds which pop when squeezed. The name \"Platycodon\" means \"flat bell\", which aptly describes the opened flowers. It grows best in full sun to partial shade and well-drained, slightly acidic soil.",
