                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.epicgardening.com/beauty-bush",
                        "snippet": "The beauty bush, now known as Linnaea amabilis, is a shrub native to parts of China and belongs to the honeysuckle family.. The beauty bush used to be scientifically classified as Kolkwitzia amabilis, named after the German botanist Richard Kolkwitz.It has since been reclassified as Linnaea amabilis.. \u201cAmabilis\u201d means \u201clovely,\u201d which seems like a compliment to the botanist, and it ...",
