                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monarda",
                        "snippet": "Monarda is a genus of flowering plants in the mint family, Lamiaceae. [3] The genus is endemic to North America. [2][4] Common names include bergamot, bee balm, horsemint, and oswego tea, the first being inspired by the fragrance of the leaves, which is reminiscent of bergamot orange (Citrus bergamia). The genus was named for the Spanish ...",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-05T02:22:00.0000000Z",
                        "primaryImageOfPage": {
