                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/flowers/bee-balm/bee-balm-care.htm",
                        "snippet": "The bee balm plant is a North American native that thrives in woodland areas. Also known as bergamot and by its botanical name Monarda, bee balm is attractive to bees, butterflies, and hummingbirds. The bee balm flower has an open, daisy-like shape, with tubular petals in shades of red, pink, purple, and white. Bee balm plants are perennial, coming back year after year to add cheerful color to ...",
