                        "snippet": "Black-Eyed Susan Rudbeckia hirta. This black-eyed susan is a knockout for gardens, known for its bright yellow petals and dark brown central cone. It is a short-lived perennial (1-2 years) but will easily reseed itself. R. Hirta is easily identified by the short hairs on its stems and leaves.",
