                        "datePublished": "2021-09-17T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Sep 17, 2021",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/flowers/bleeding-heart/indoor-bleeding...",
                        "snippet": "An ideal location for your indoor bleeding heart is an area that has bright, indirect light. Filtered sun will work well, and some morning sun is beneficial. Try and avoid hot, mid-day sun indoors. Another concern you should have in growing bleeding heart as a houseplant is humidity. These plants, like ferns, enjoy high humidity.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T03:47:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Bleeding-heart+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4966111901450941&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=-bm3_ukX3KnSU_wTIvuqvReu81nzpsbM",
