                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/dicentra-eximia",
                        "snippet": "Fringed bleeding heart is a beautiful, native perennial plant occurring on forest floors, rocky woods and ledges in the Appalachian Mountains. It prefers rich, moist, well-drained soil and does not like wet winter soil. The fern-like foliage and blooms appear in spring and bloom time can continue into summer. In hot climates, it may stop ...",
