                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/flowers/bleeding-heart/winterizing-a...",
                        "snippet": "It is because of this, bleeding heart winter care technically starts months before the first fall frost. When the flowers of your bleeding heart plant fade, cut back their stems to an inch or two (2.5-5 cm.) above ground. Keep watering the foliage. Eventually, the foliage will die back too. This might happen naturally in the summer, or it might ...",
