                        "snippet": "Noteworthy Characteristics. Geranium sanguineum, commonly called bloody cranesbill or bloodred geranium, is an herbaceous, clump-forming perennial that typically grows in a mound to 9-12\u201d tall with white-hairy trailing stems spreading over time to as much as 24\u201d wide.It is native to Europe and Asia. It is perhaps the most common species of geranium grown in the U.S. today.",
