                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Festuca_glauca",
                        "snippet": "Common names include blue fescue, blue mountain grass, and grey fescue. It was originally described by French naturalist Dominique Villars.. The genus name Festuca means 'straw', and is a name that was used by Pliny the Elder. 'Festuca' also refers to a rod used to manumit Romans from slavery to freedom. [2]The species name glauca is derived from Latin and means 'with a white or greyish bloom ...",
