                        "snippet": "Sage is an attractive culinary herb. Salvia officinalis is an aromatic, rather woody perennial shrub in the mint family (Lamiaceae) native to the shores of the northern Mediterranean. Its common names include culinary sage, common garden sage, or garden sage. The word \u201csage\u201d has come to mean \u201cwise\u201d or \u201ca wise or learned person.\u201d It\u2019s scientific name, Salvia, means \u201cto be in ...",
