                        "displayUrl": "https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/achillea-millefolium",
                        "snippet": "Yarrow is a herbaceous perennial in the Asteraceae (daisy) family Introduced to America from Europe in colonial times. This plant prefers well-drained soil and full sun and it is often found naturalizing in fields and along roadsides. It is a wonderful wildlife plant that attracts butterflies. Makes excellent cut or dried arrangements.",
