                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.6",
                        "name": "Common Yarrow (Achillea millefolium L.) Plant Guide",
                        "url": "https://www.nrcs.usda.gov/plantmaterials/mtpmcpg13974.pdf",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.nrcs.usda.gov/plantmaterials/mtpmcpg13974.pdf",
                        "snippet": "Plant common yarrow at 1 to 2 pounds per acre into warm soil at 1\u20444 inch depth and 3 feet apart in a sunny area (Sanders, 1905; Clark, 1998; Hebel et al., 1998; Noller, 2001; Schalau, 2009; Alaback et al., 2017). If broadcast seeding, double the seeding rate. Germination occurs within one or two weeks.",
