                        "displayUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zinnia",
                        "snippet": "Zinnia is a genus of plants of the tribe Heliantheae within the family Asteraceae. [3] [4] They are native to scrub and dry grassland in an area stretching from the Southwestern United States to South America, with a centre of diversity in Mexico.Members of the genus are notable for their solitary long-stemmed 12 petal flowers that come in a variety of bright colors.",
