                        "displayUrl": "https://www.thespruce.com/zinnias-a-burst-of-hot-flower-colors-from-zinnias-1402919",
                        "snippet": "Here's how to propagate zinnias by taking a cutting, which is best done in spring: Cut a healthy, 6-inch stem that's not yet flowering. Remove the leaves from the bottom half of the cutting. Put the cutting in water and wait for roots. Once roots are a few inches long, plant the cutting in moist soil or directly into the ground.",
