                        "snippet": "Hemerocallis, commonly known as daylily due to each flower\u2019s one-day lifespan, is a genus of perennial plants in the family Asphodelaceae. Native to Eurasia, these plants are cultivated worldwide for their showy flowers and hardiness. A key fact about daylilies is their immense popularity among breeders and hobbyists.",
