                        "snippet": "Dusty Miller was a British prisoner of war (POW) in Thailand conscripted to work on the Burma Railway during the last three and a half years of World War II. His life and death is attested to in Gordon's book. Miller was a gardener from Newcastle and a Methodist.Like Gordon, he was in the Argyll and Sutherland Highlanders, but was drafted into the Military Police or \"Red Caps\".",
