                        "snippet": "Propagating Eastern Redbud Bush . Eastern redbud bush is best propagated from seed. Stem cuttings are another propagation method, but it is mostly unsuccessful. They have a moderate growth rate; in favorable conditions, expect yours to grow about 7 to 10 feet in the first five or six years.",
