                        "displayUrl": "https://www.srs.fs.usda.gov/pubs/misc/ag_654/volume_2/cercis/canadensis.htm",
                        "snippet": "Eastern redbud is a strikingly conspicuous tree in the spring because it flowers before other tree leaves form. The wood is heavy, hard, and close-grained, but because of the small size and irregular shape of the tree it is of no commercial value as a source of lumber. This tree is most valued as an ornamental and is extensively planted.",
