                        "displayUrl": "https://www.thespruce.com/maiden-grass-miscanthus-sinensis-gracillimus-2132484",
                        "snippet": "Depending on your plant's size, it may be heavy, and you may need assistance. Plunge a sharp shovel edge into the root ball, splitting it in half. Divide the halves in half, if possible. Plant each as a new plant at least 3 to 6 feet apart. Maiden grass needs its room since clumps get large. Drench with water.",
