                        "snippet": "Having originated in Asia, this grass has numerous cultivars, although some are considered weedy and invasive in the southeastern United States. It is seen most commonly along roadsides and disturbed areas. This clumping grass grows up to 12 feet tall in all types of soil and in all but the shadiest of environments.",
