                        "snippet": "Fan Flower is a herbaceous, flowering perennial with a sprawling habit native to the arid and semi-arid areas of Australia. It is hardy in a narrow range of USDA zones (zones 10 and 11) where it thrives in hot and dry summer climates, but it can be grown as an annual in North Carolina. It can also be taken indoors over winter if desired.",
