                        "snippet": "Fairy Fan-flower. Scaevola aemula R.Br.. Scaevola aemula is a member of the family Goodenaceae. The widely known common name is Fairy Fan-flower, which pertains to the small size of the S. aemula plants.. It is distributed along the New South Wales and Victorian coastlines where it can be found in the form of a low growing perennial herb.",
