                        "snippet": "This makes scaevola eye-catching even when it is not in flower. Flowers. Without a doubt, the most striking feature of this plant is its flowers. They appear in clusters that arise at the ends of the stems. Each of the flowers has five petals that are partially fused, and they have a central spur. This is what gives them that particular fan shape.",
