                        "displayUrl": "https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/achillea/common-name/fern-leaf-yarrow",
                        "snippet": "Common Yarrow has dense, white flower heads that appear in compact clusters at the top of the stem. The flower head has 20 to 25 ray flowers. Other varieties may have colors including gold, white, pink, and cerise red. Their bloom season is from late spring, summer, into fall. Leaves: Woody Plant Leaf Characteristics: Deciduous Leaf Color: Green",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-10-28T23:11:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Fern-leaf+Yarrow+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4971162788496088&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=gfz-QCxrmZbUn-BSPQug_UE8WY8j4xBw",
