                        "displayUrl": "https://gardenerspath.com/plants/flowers/grow-yarrow",
                        "snippet": "Achillea spp.. Yarrow, Achillea spp., is a semi-evergreen flowering perennial in the aster, or Asteraceae family. Suitable for growers in USDA Hardiness Zones 3 to 9, it has corymb, or flattened, flower heads with densely clustered blossoms in shades of pink, red, white, and yellow.. In this article, you\u2019ll learn all you need to know to cultivate and maintain yarrow in your garden.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-03T04:03:00.0000000Z",
