                        "displayUrl": "https://www.thespruce.com/achillea-growing-yarrow-in-the-perennial-garden-1402830",
                        "snippet": "Common yarrow (Achillea millefolium) is a perennial flowering plant that goes by many names, like gordaldo, poor man's pepper, and thousand leaf.In the southwestern U.S., you'll hear it referred to as a plumajillo, Spanish for \"little feather\" due to the feathery shape and lacy texture of the plant's aromatic leaves.Yarrow can grow to reach more than 3 feet tall during the course of a growing ...",
