                                "snippet": "A relative of the pansy, field pansies are easily distinguished. They are smaller than the pansy, less than 1\" in diameter. The plant size is also smaller, however, they make up for their small size by producing more blooms than the pansy. Young leaves develop from a basal rosette. They are rounded to oval with a shallowly toothed margin.",
