                        "snippet": "Ornamental cabbage, also called flowering cabbage, has smooth, wavy edges with bright rosette centers of pink, purple, red, or white leaves. It grows about a foot (31 cm.) wide and up to 15 inches (38 cm.) tall with a mounding habit. Though considered edible-- it has a very bitter taste-- ornamental cabbage is more often used as a food garnish.",
