                        "displayUrl": "https://www.weekand.com/home-garden/article/common-name-hosta-18009503.php",
                        "snippet": "Scientific names are always written with the first letter of the genus name capitalized and the species name lowercase, with some exceptions. In scientific or trade writing both parts of the name are italicized. \"Hosta\" was first used as the genus name for this group of perennials in 1812, to honor Austrian botanist Nicholas Thomas Host.",
