                        "snippet": "Description: Fragrant sumac belongs to the Anacardiaceae family. A straggling to upright native shrub 6 to 8 feet tall rarely tree like in appearance. This shrub occurs singly or in dense thickets that may be connected by rhizomes. Root systems are deep and extensively branched.",
