                        "displayUrl": "https://www.colorado.edu/asmagazine/2020/01/07/smooth-sumac-has-edible-berries-and...",
                        "snippet": "The genus Rhuscontains about 35 species that are native to North America, but only one other species is native to Colorado\u2014fragrant sumac, Rhus trilobata. Both glabra and trilobata have rhizomes that send up young stems and this form of asexual reproduction produces clones of sumac. Smooth and fragrant sumac are easy to distinguish.",
