                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?taxonid=277481",
                        "snippet": "Tagetes patula, commonly called French marigold, is a compact annual that typically grow 6-12\u201d tall and feature single, semi-double, double or crested, fragrant flowers (1-2\u201d diameter) in shades of yellow, orange, red and bicolor. Pinnate leaves with toothed, lance-shaped leaflets are aromatic. Genus named for an Etruscan deity, Tages.",
