                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Oct 4, 2024",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.thespruce.com/growing-bleeding-heart-plants-1402834",
                        "snippet": "Plant a bleeding heart in partial shade and rich, well-draining soil. Plant the bleeding heart's bare roots so the crown is about 1 to 2 inches below the soil. If it's planted too deeply, the crown may rot. Protect these delicate flowers from strong winds by placing a bleeding heart in an area with a windbreak and some sun protection.",
