                        "displayUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dicentra_eximia",
                        "snippet": "Dicentra eximia (wild or fringed bleeding-heart, turkey-corn) is a flowering plant with fernlike leaves and oddly shaped flowers native to the Appalachian Mountains.It is similar to the Pacific bleeding-heart (Dicentra formosa), which grows on the Pacific Coast.Dicentra eximia is a perennial herb in the Papaveraceae family. [2]",
