                        "snippet": "Genus name comes from the Latin name meaning lily. 'Casa Blanca' is a popular oriental hybrid cultivar that features pure white flowers (to 8-10\" wide) with contrasting reddish-brown anthers. Blooms in mid-summer on rigid stems rising 3-4' tall. Flowers are very fragrant. Excellent fresh cut flower.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T11:44:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Garden+Lily+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4563097941311987&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=Ekb3yeNOnrYbDtZx_Tx3axFEMlwq0NK5",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Missouri Botanical Garden"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.17",
                        "name": "Lily (Lilium 'Farolito') in the Lilies Database - Garden.org",
                        "url": "https://garden.org/plants/view/144282/Lily-Lilium-Farolito/",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://garden.org/plants/view/144282/Lily-Lilium-Farolito",
                        "snippet": "Other info: Species lilies will come true from seed; cultivars and hybrids will not. Propagation: Other methods: Offsets. Other: Bulb scaling. Containers: Suitable in 3 gallon or larger. Needs repotting every 2 to 3 years. Needs excellent drainage in pots.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-10-28T16:15:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Garden+Lily+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4638272754352502&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=EQJDOa78x9g9PkAJ103cCq-P69dJC4aN",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "The National Gardening Association"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.18",
                        "name": "PlantFiles: The Largest Plant Identification Reference Guide - Dave's ...",
                        "url": "https://davesgarden.com/guides/pf/go/399",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://davesgarden.com/guides/pf/go/399",
                        "snippet": "west Houston, TX (Zone 9a) | January 2007 | positive. This particular Zephyranthes likes wet, acidic, rich soil enriched with leaf mould. Offsets well and sets and grows fast from seed. B. ButterflyGardnr. Orlando, FL (Zone 9b) | December 2002 | positive. This plant is easy to grow from bulb. Blooms appear mainly after rains.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-03T04:02:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Garden+Lily+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4715590754107850&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=BfnR7uGqEitgZ1AeXvlXlLVCDIZcCJlz",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Dave's Garden"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.19",
                        "name": "Lily Plant Companions - Learn About Companion Planting With Lily ...",
                        "url": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/bulbs/lily/companions-for-lilies.htm",
                        "datePublished": "2023-02-15T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Feb 15, 2023",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/bulbs/lily/companions-for-lilies.htm",
                        "snippet": "Hydrangea. Weigela. Rose of Sharon. Bush honeysuckle. Smoke bush. Be sure to give lilies plenty of space of their own, and don't crowd them with companion plants. Lily bulbs are soft and tender, and the strong, aggressive roots of other plants can pierce these bulbs, damaging or even killing them.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-03T22:35:00.0000000Z",
