                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://todayshomeowner.com/lawn-garden/guides/verbena",
                        "snippet": "Verbena prefers the soil to dry out between waterings. Once established, it can handle a bit of drought, but to get the best blooms, aim for about an inch of water per week. During dry spells, give them a deep watering once a week, and make sure to water at the base, avoiding wetting the foliage to prevent mildew.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T17:25:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Garden+Verbena+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4984039103267362&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=7iZz0e5UVfvaeunhvAdbMa4IFTZxtiPi",
                        "language": "en",
