                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?taxonid=263340",
                        "snippet": "Noteworthy Characteristics. Verbena \u00d7 hybrida, commonly called garden verbena, is a short-lived perennial that is grown in St. Louis as an annual.It is noted for its profuse bloom of small five-petaled flowers in rounded clusters (to 3\u201d wide) from late spring to fall on plants ranging in size from mat-forming/trailing (to 10\u201d tall) to bushy/upright (to 20: tall).",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T14:58:00.0000000Z",
