                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/verbena-bonariensis",
                        "snippet": "Tall verbena is a tall upright plant with rounded clusters of small purple flowers, that measure 2 to 3 inches in diameter on long wispy stems. Each flower is about a 0.25-inch purple tube. The leaves are primarily at the base of the plant and form a mounded rosette of green, lance-shaped leaves with serrated margins.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-05T06:59:00.0000000Z",
