                        "snippet": "Noteworthy Characteristics. Muhlenbergia capillaris, commonly called pink muhlygrass or pink hair grass, is a clump-forming, warm season, perennial grass that is noted for its attractive summer foliage and spectacular clouds of fall flowers.It is native to prairies, pine barrens, and open woodlands from Massachusetts to Kansas south to Florida and Texas.",
