                        "displayUrl": "www.hostalists.org/hosta_list_rhih.php",
                        "snippet": "The Hosta Dictionary posted by the American Hosta Society describes rhizomatous hostas as those which have long-reaching, underground horizontal stems and a loosely spreading habit. When asked which hostas are rhizomatous, W. George Schmid provided the following information: \"The short answer is that all hostas are rhizomatous plants.\"",
