                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://gardenerspath.com/plants/flowers/best-astilbe-varieties",
                        "snippet": "There are 18 different species in the Astilbe genus and numerous hybrid cultivars. The most commonly grown species in home gardens include A. chinensis, A. japonica, A. thunbergii, and A. simplicifolia along with a large number of hybrids.. In the late 19th and early 20th century, George Arends, a plant breeder from Germany developed named hybrid cultivars known collectively as A. x arendsii.",
