                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.thespruce.com/growing-astible-plants-1402833",
                        "snippet": "Astilbe plants need phosphorus to bloom, so choose a fertilizer with the makeup of 5-10-5 or 10-10-10. Rake the fertilizer into the soil two weeks before you plant, or sprinkle a few granules onto the soil after the astilbe has been planted. Once the plant is established, fertilize every spring when the soil is moist.",
