                        "displayUrl": "https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/astilbe-x-arendsii",
                        "snippet": "They grow about 24 to 36 inches tall and 18-24 inches wide. The showy flowers are excellent for floral cuttings or use in a dried arrangement. Astilbes are native to China, Japan, and Korea. Astilbe x arendsii are hybrids and are the result of crosses between Astilbe Chinensis, Astilbe Japonica, Astilbe thunergii, and Astilbe astilboides.",
