                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.illinoiswildflowers.info/grasses/plants/ind_grass.htm",
                        "snippet": "Indian Grass (Sorghastrum nutans) Indian Grass. Grass family (Poaceae) Description: This perennial grass is 3-7' tall. It typically consists of a dense tuft of flowering culms and their deciduous leaves. The culms are terete, glabrous, pale green or pale yellow, and unbranched. Alternate leaves occur primarily along the lower one-half of each culm.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-03T08:33:00.0000000Z",
                        "primaryImageOfPage": {
