                        "displayUrl": "https://www.guide-to-houseplants.com/ivy-geranium.html",
                        "snippet": "Move your plant to a pot 1-2 inches (2.5-5 cm) larger when you see roots growing through the drainage holes. Or keep it in the same pot and just give it fresh potting mix. Give it a winter rest. Overwinter geraniums in a cool basement or garage with a minimum temperature of 50\u00b0F/10\u00b0C.",
