                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.nature-and-garden.com/gardening/ivy-geranium.html",
                        "snippet": "Ivy geranium can keep from one year to the next, but regrowth isn\u2019t guaranteed, unlike conventional geraniums. At the season\u2019s end, if they are in pots or garden boxes: Prune your ivy geranium back to \u2154 their original length. Place them in a shed out of the cold and reduce the watering. In winter, watering once a month is enough.",
