                        "snippet": "Care of Japanese Iris. Once planted and placed in the pond, Japanese iris care is minimal. Limit fertilization to plants with a well-developed root system, and only use plant food that is high in nitrogen. Japanese iris care will include the division of the rhizomes every three to four years. Crowded plants tend to offer fewer blooms.",
