                        "snippet": "The Japanese lilac (Syringa reticulata) is a deciduous tree-form lilac attractive enough to serve as a specimen.It has a moderate growth rate, an upright growing habit, and a rounded shape. It is a mid-size tree belonging to the olive family and grown for the panicles of white flowers that are 6 to 12 inches long, which it bears for about two weeks in early summer.",
