                        "webSearchUrl": "https://www.bing.com/entityexplore?q=Syringa+reticulata&filters=sid:%22cba034ba-0e42-4196-df05-b938111abb5f%22&elv=AXXfrEiqqD9r3GuelwApulpKCfKXvP1aQ5OLC4!k1PPJf7!XPRBkgsQeV0u3oDkHdlqv84!kjmNXkNr2dR0akzf8yJvDPx3O8I0vf8M!gqkX",
                        "name": "Syringa reticulata",
                        "image": {
                            "name": "Syringa reticulata",
                            "thumbnailUrl": "http://www.bing.com/th?id=OSK.8aeb4c868161f376cb04e705de1bc94a&w=110&h=110&c=7",
                            "provider": [
                                {
                                    "_type": "Organization",
                                    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syringa_reticulata"
                                }
                            ],
                            "hostPageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2f/Syringa_reticulata_USDA1.jpg",
                            "width": 110,
                            "height": 110,
                            "sourceWidth": 1125,
                            "sourceHeight": 1497
                        },
                        "description": "Syringa reticulata, the Japanese tree lilac, is a species of flowering plant in the family Oleaceae native to eastern Asia, which is grown as an ornamental in Europe and North America. It is a deciduous small tree growing to a height of 12 m, rarely to 15 m, with a trunk up to 30 cm, rarely 40 cm in diameter; it is the largest species of lilac, and the only one that regularly makes a small tree rather than a shrub. The leaves are elliptic-acute, 2.5\u201315 cm long and 1\u20138 cm broad, with an entire margin, and a roughish texture with slightly impressed veins. The flowers are white or creamy-white, the corolla with a tubular base 0.16\u20130.24\" long and a four-lobed apex 0.12\u20130.24\" across, and a strong fragrance; they are produced in broad panicles 5\u201330 cm long and 3\u201320 cm broad in early summer. The fruit is a dry, smooth, brown capsule, splitting in two to release the two winged seeds.",
                        "entityPresentationInfo": {
                            "entityScenario": "DominantEntity",
                            "entityTypeHints": [
                                "Generic"
                            ],
                            "entityTypeDisplayHint": "Species of plant"
                        },
                        "bingId": "cba034ba-0e42-4196-df05-b938111abb5f"
                    }
                ]
