                        "name": "How to Grow and Care for Joe Pye Weed - The Spruce",
                        "url": "https://www.thespruce.com/joe-pye-weed-eupatorium-purpureum-1402848",
                        "thumbnailUrl": "https://www.bing.com/th?id=OIP.YFW9QwxW4MfYx5Y4Ez2v6QHaE8&w=80&h=80&c=1&pid=5.1",
                        "datePublished": "2024-05-09T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "May 9, 2024",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.thespruce.com/joe-pye-weed-eupatorium-purpureum-1402848",
                        "snippet": "Joe Pye weed is a late-blooming wildflower with tiny mauve or pink-purple flowers blooming in large clusters atop tall, thick stems. Joe Pye weed grows naturally in sites that have somewhat moist soil, such as near streams or in drainage ditches. requires full sun or partial shade, well-drained soil, and can grow in cold or warm conditions until frost hits.",
