                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardenersworld.com/how-to/grow-plants/how-to-grow-ladys-mantle",
                        "snippet": "Lady\u2019s mantle is a tolerant, easy to grow plant that needs little maintenance once established. Cut back faded stems after flowering. Do this before the seeds ripen to prevent it self-seeding. If the plant is looking straggly, cut stems to the ground to encourage fresh new growth to form. Once growth has died back in autumn, cut to ground level.",
