                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/alchemilla-mollis",
                        "snippet": "The genus name, Alchemilla, may be a Latinized form of an Arabic word. The species name, mollis, means soft which is an accurate description of the leaves of this plant. They are soft and downy, up to 6 inches wide, circular in shape with 9 \u2013 11 shallow lobes. The color is a soft pale green. They form a dense mound up to 12 inches high and wide.",
