                        "datePublished": "2024-05-13T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "May 13, 2024",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.thespruce.com/lilac-bushes-growing-tips-2132722",
                        "snippet": "Lilac bushes tend to spread through off shoots that grow from the base of the plant. If you want to propagate a new lilac bush, dig up a shoot while making sure to keep the roots intact. Sever it from the main plant and replant it in a new location. This will keep the bush from unwanted spread and also create a new plant to care for.",
