                        "displayUrl": "https://extension.umd.edu/agnr.umd.edu/agnr.umd.edu/extension.umd.edu/resource/lilac...",
                        "snippet": "Key points. Common lilac (Syringa vulgaris) is a woody shrub grown for its extremely fragrant flowers in mid to late spring, depending on the location.There are several species of lilacs but Syringa vulgaris is the most commonly planted species in Maryland.; Named cultivars can have a wide range of flower colors including lilac, purple, white, pink, and a reddish hue.",
