                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.13",
                        "name": "Tips For Growing Lilac Bushes | Gardening Know How",
                        "url": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/shrubs/lilac/lilac-care-growing-and-planting-lilac-bush-plants.htm",
                        "datePublished": "2021-04-12T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Apr 12, 2021",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/shrubs/lilac/lilac-care-growing-and...",
                        "snippet": "Spring or fall is the best time for planting lilac bushes. Situate the lilac with its roots spread vertically in the ground and make the hole both deep and wide enough to accommodate them. If planting more than one lilac bush, space them at least 5 feet (1.5 m.) apart to prevent overcrowding, even if you plan to use them as hedges for privacy.",
