                        "snippet": "Planting and Caring for Lily of the Valley. Plant lily of the valley from nursery transplants or divisions in early spring. Amend poor soils with compost, manure and peat moss. If your soil is very alkaline, add some sulfur to lower the soil pH. Space lily of the valley plants 12 inches apart and water frequently to keep the soil slightly moist ...",
