                        "snippet": "Common Types of Lily of the Valley. Common lily of the valley (Convallaria majalis) has dark green leaves, tops out at about 10 inches (25 cm.) in height, and produces small, extremely fragrant, white flowers.As long as it\u2019s contained from taking over the garden, you can\u2019t go wrong with this variety. There are, however, a large number of interesting cultivars that set themselves apart.",
