                        "snippet": "Known by the botanical name Convallaria majalis, lily-of-the-valley is a fragrant woodland flower in the Asparagaceae family. It\u2019s native to Europe, North America, and some parts of Asia with cool climates. Usually blooming in spring to early summer, these flowers are cultivated in many temperate regions of the world, but aren\u2019t able to survive hot weather.",
