                        "snippet": "1. Grow lobelia from seed or transplant. Start seeds indoors 6-8 weeks before planting outside. Press seeds into the soil but do not cover; they need light to germinate. When buying transplants, look for compact, healthy transplants with few blooms, stocky stems, and deep-green leaves.",
