                        "snippet": "Lobelia is a large genus of almost 400 species of annuals, perennials, aquatics, and shrubs from around the globe, but especially the Americas. There is great variability within the genus, but all species have two-lipped, tubular flowers, often very brightly colored. Grow perennials in a border or at waterside, annuals as edging or in containers, and aquatics in a wildlife pond.",
