                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.18",
                        "name": "GREAT BLUE LOBELIA - USDA Plants Database",
                        "url": "https://plants.usda.gov/DocumentLibrary/plantguide/pdf/pg_losi.pdf",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://plants.usda.gov/DocumentLibrary/plantguide/pdf/pg_losi.pdf",
                        "snippet": "Protect the plants from deer. Great blue lobelia will usually bloom in the first year. Allow the plants to self-sow. They are heavy feeders, so compost or apply granular fertilizer when they begin growth. Propagation by cuttings: Take two node stem cuttings (4-6 inches) before the flowers open and remove the lower leaf and half the upper leaf.",
