                        "snippet": "maiden pink Small inflorescences of maiden pink (Dianthus deltoides). (more) Pinks are mostly short herbaceous perennials, many of which are tufted or mat-forming hardy evergreens. There are also some annual forms. The small but showy and often fragrant flowers are mostly pink to deep rose, with some being red, purple, white, or yellow.",
