                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Apr 28, 2022",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://thegardenmagazine.com/how-to-grow-moss-phlox",
                        "snippet": "Propagating Moss Phlox . Division, stem cuttings, and rooted stems are all straightforward ways to grow Moss phlox. Cuttings are a very straightforward way to reproduce plants if done correctly, as they root quickly after a few months. All you have to do is remove a 6-inch-long portion from a rooted stem or a lateral branch at the tip of the plant.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-10-09T15:05:00.0000000Z",
