                        "snippet": "Long considered one of the best rock garden perennnials, Creeping Phlox quickly spreads and blooms profusely in April and May. Also called Flowering Moss, Moss Phlox, Ground Pink and Moss Pinks. This is an evergreen groundcover that reaches a height of 6\u201d but can spread out to 36\u201d at maturity. Creeping phlox is native to eastern woodlands.",
