                        "displayUrl": "https://growingthehomegarden.com/moss-phlox-why-you-should-plant-phlox-subulata",
                        "snippet": "To prevent root rot, plant moss phlox in well-draining soil and avoid overwatering. In general try to keep the plant\u2019s foliage dry to help prevent the spread of diseases. In terms of pests, aphids and spider mites can sometimes target Phlox subulata. These tiny insects can suck sap from the plant, causing damage to the foliage.",
