                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gfloutdoors.com/moss-verbena-care-everything-you-need-to-know",
                        "snippet": "Moss verbena needs regular watering, but do not water it excessively. The soil should be kept moist but not wet. If the soil is too wet, the plant could develop root rot. This plant grows best in slightly acidic soil with a pH of 6.0 to 6.8. You can test the pH of your soil with a pH meter or soil testing kit.",
