                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/flowers/zinnia/how-to-grow-creeping-zinnia...",
                        "snippet": "Learning how to grow creeping zinnia is simple. Grow the plants from seed direct planted in the ground in autumn or sow indoors in late winter. When planting seeds, space them 6 to 9 (15-23 cm.) inches apart. Some local nurseries carry inexpensive seedlings. Plant in a full sun area where several flowers display on a bushy, multi-stemmed plant.",
