                        "name": "Mexican Zinnia Plant Care: Tips On Growing Mexican Zinnia Flowers",
                        "url": "https://plantcaretoday.com/mexican-zinnia-plant.html",
                        "thumbnailUrl": "https://www.bing.com/th?id=OIP.Yu1His03dOxCK6AzWBTy0wHaD4&w=80&h=80&c=1&pid=5.1",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://plantcaretoday.com/mexican-zinnia-plant.html",
                        "snippet": "Sow the seeds in well-drained soil at least 4 to 6 weeks before the last spring frost. Once the plants are ready around mid-May, and the weather has warmed up, plant them in the ground, placing them at least 9\u201d inches apart. Propagating by cutting. Choose 5 to 6 healthy shoots having at least one node left on them.",
