                        "displayUrl": "https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/symphyotrichum-novae-angliae",
                        "snippet": "Common Name (s): New England Aster is a herbaceous perennial that may grow 3 to 7 feet tall. The leaves are alternate, rough, and hairy. The leaves have a smooth margin. The stem is fuzzy. Large, purple flowers with a yellow center mature from August to October. The herb produces a dry seed (achene) that matures in the late fall.",
