                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symphyotrichum_novae-angliae",
                        "snippet": "Symphyotrichum novae-angliae (formerly Aster novae-angliae) is a species of flowering plant in the aster family native to central and eastern North America. Commonly known as New England aster, [4] hairy Michaelmas-daisy, [5] or Michaelmas daisy, [6] it is a perennial, herbaceous plant usually between 30 and 120 centimeters (1 and 4 feet) tall and 60 to 90 cm (2 to 3 ft) wide.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-05T07:16:00.0000000Z",
                        "primaryImageOfPage": {
