                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?kempercode=...",
                        "snippet": "Noteworthy Characteristics. Symphyotrichum novae-angliae, commonly called New England aster, is a Missouri native perennial which occurs in moist prairies, meadows, thickets, low valleys and stream banks (Steyermark) throughout the State.It is a stout, leafy plant typically growing 3-6' tall with a robust, upright habit. Features a profuse bloom of daisy-like asters (to 1.5\" diameter) with ...",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-05T03:27:00.0000000Z",
