                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.fs.usda.gov/wildflowers/plant-of-the-week/symphyotrichum_novae-angliae.shtml",
                        "snippet": "New England Aster (Symphyotrichum novae-angliae (L.) G.L. Nesom)By David Taylor. New England aster is a member of the Asteraceae (Aster or Composite) family. Until recently, it was placed in the genus Aster, a then large and complex group.Its name Symphyotrichum, means \u2018united hairs\u2019, and novae-angliae, \u2018New England.\u2019The old name Aster meant star in reference to the shape of the flower.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-10-26T14:37:00.0000000Z",
                        "primaryImageOfPage": {
