                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "May 13, 2022",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://extension.psu.edu/rain-garden-plants-new-england-aster",
                        "snippet": "One-page informational sheet with details and pictures of New England aster (Symphyotrichum novae-angliae). Distinguishable from other asters by its larger compound flowers (up to 1.5 inches). Flowers vary from pink to purple and have golden centers. Leaves are 4 to 5 inches long, very hairy, lance-oblong in shape, and have mostly smooth margins.",
