                        "thumbnailUrl": "https://www.bing.com/th?id=OIP.kl7hsO55mTzOUjkaEgIk3wHaFP&w=80&h=80&c=1&pid=5.1",
                        "datePublished": "2023-08-16T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Aug 16, 2023",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.birdsandblooms.com/gardening/flower-gardening/new-england-aster",
                        "snippet": "If you have a butterfly garden, you should definitely consider growing aster plants. Common name: New England aster. Scientific name: Symphyotrichum novae-angliae. Growing zone: 4 to 8. Light needs: Full sun. Soil: Moist. Size: 3 to 6 feet tall, 2 to 3 feet wide. Attracts: Bees, butterflies and birds. Courtesy Sean McGuinn.",
