                        "displayUrl": "https://gobotany.nativeplanttrust.org/species/symphyotrichum/novae-angliae",
                        "snippet": "New England American-aster and its cultivars are widely used in horticulture, and consequently escapes may be rather common. The species has been introduced outside its range in North America and Europe. It is a distinctive species having more ray flowers than other America-asters (45-100 per flower head), of a deep red-purple.",
