                        "snippet": "Wildlife: New England aster is known for attracting butterflies and moths to areas where it is found growing. This is a good bee plant providing nectar in the autumn. Most species in this genus seem to be immune to the predications of rabbits (Thomas 1990). erect stems in clumps, stems 0.8 to 2 meters, densely spreading pubescent, thirty or ...",
