                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://gardenerspath.com/plants/flowers/grow-new-england-aster",
                        "snippet": "Use clean pruning shears to cut a six-inch stem from your plant, removing the leaves from the bottom 3-4 inches. Dip the stem into water and then into a rooting hormone powder. Fill a seed starting container with potting medium, and plant the cutting 2-3 inches deep.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T09:35:00.0000000Z",
                        "primaryImageOfPage": {
