                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/flowers/asters/growing-new-england-asters.htm",
                        "snippet": "The New England aster will germinate in 21 to 45 days at a soil temperature of 65 to 75 degrees F. (8-24 C.). These late summer through early fall bloomers spread 2 to 4 feet (0.6-1 m.) with a height of 1 to 6 feet (0.3-2 m.). When planting make sure to provide good air circulation, keeping in mind the large spreading area.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T23:30:00.0000000Z",
