                        "snippet": "New England aster (Aster novae-angliae) New England aster is a gorgeous, tall fall bloomer that attracts numerous pollinators and hosts the Cresent butterfly. Because it loses its lower leaves as it grows, it's best in meadow gardens or as a backdrop to shorter plants like Rudbeckia. Return to Plant Search Home. Height: 2-4 ft.",
