                        "snippet": "New Guinea Impatiens prefer slightly acidic soil with a pH range of 6.0 to 6.5. Fill the pot with the potting mix, leaving enough space for the plant\u2019s root ball. Planting: Gently remove the New Guinea Impatiens plant from its nursery container, being careful not to damage the roots. Place the plant in the pot, ensuring it is positioned at ...",
