                        "snippet": "Impatiens (Impatiens walleriana) are one of the most popular bedding plants in the United States. They are ideal for containers, hanging baskets, and beds. Impatiens have glossy, medium-green leaves. Flowers are 1 to 2 inches in diameter, may be single or double, and come in a wide variety of colors. Plants commonly grow 12 to 18 inches tall.",
