                        "snippet": "Oakleaf hydrangea also referred to as Hydrangea quercifolia is a species of flowering plant in the family Hydrangeaceae. It is native to the Southeastern United States, in woodland habitats from North Carolina west to Tennessee and south to Florida and Louisiana. The plant can grow up to 8 feet high and between 4 to 6 feet wide.",
