                        "thumbnailUrl": "https://www.bing.com/th?id=OIP.pvgDU56Kb1Xf5NCKtCs8egHaJ4&w=80&h=80&c=1&pid=5.1",
                        "datePublished": "2021-06-21T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Jun 21, 2021",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/edible/vegetables/pepper/grow-ornamental-pepper...",
                        "snippet": "How to Grow Ornamental Pepper Plants. Start ornamental peppers indoors in small individual pots filled with potting soil or seed starting medium. Bury the seeds \u00bc to \u00bd inch (6 mm. to 1 cm.) deep. Allow one to two weeks for the seeds to germinate and another six to eight weeks for the seedlings to reach transplanting size.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-03T05:04:00.0000000Z",
                        "primaryImageOfPage": {
