                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Apr 6, 2023",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.healthygreensavvy.com/how-identify-purslane",
                        "snippet": "LEAVES. Purslane has smooth, fleshy leaves that are pretty recognizable. Many people find purslane\u2019s succulent leaves similar in look to jade plant (Crassula ovata), a common houseplant that is NOT edible.Purslane leaves are elongated ovals with rounded tips and tend to appear in star-shaped clusters of 4 at the end of the stem branches.",
