                        "datePublished": "2023-04-04T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Apr 4, 2023",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://gardenerspath.com/plants/herbs/grow-purslane",
                        "snippet": "I think cultivated purslane has a less bitter, sweeter flavor. Cultivated plants, which grow in USDA Hardiness Zones 5 to 10, usually have larger leaves and grow in a more upright form. That\u2019s handy, come harvest time. Propagation. Purslane is typically propagated from seed, but you can also grow it from stem cuttings, divisions, or transplants.",
