                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.2",
                        "name": "What Are the Different Types of Purslane Plant | Live to Plant",
                        "url": "https://livetoplant.com/what-are-the-different-types-of-purslane-plant/",
                        "datePublished": "2023-07-15T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Jul 15, 2023",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://livetoplant.com/what-are-the-different-types-of-purslane-plant",
                        "snippet": "It also contains high levels of antioxidants and omega-3 fatty acids. Big-leaf purslane is easy to grow from seeds or cuttings and thrives in warm climates with well-drained soil. 4. Red-Stemmed Purslane (Portulaca oleracea var. rubra) Red-stemmed purslane is a unique variety of purslane that is characterized by its reddish stems and green leaves.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-04T18:26:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Ornamental+Purslane+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4604101997494330&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=1Kc8_XaT5XEttBMen4M6F5518EDWyT0L",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Live to Plant"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.3",
                        "name": "All About Purslane - Garden.org - The National Gardening Association",
                        "url": "https://garden.org/ideas/view/Boopaints/43/All-About-Purslane/",
                        "thumbnailUrl": "https://www.bing.com/th?id=OIP.cfNs5TgvS2z-qFGMUr-PLgHaLE&w=80&h=80&c=1&pid=5.1",
                        "datePublished": "2010-03-28T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Mar 28, 2010",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://garden.org/ideas/view/Boopaints/43",
                        "snippet": "Purslane is my favorite summer plant and I start looking for its appearance in the Phoenix nurseries in late May. Originally coming from India, it was grown as a food source many centuries ago. It is considered one of the foods from the Biblical period, is rich in vitamin A, C and E, and has the most Omega-3 fatty acids of any leafy vegetable.Now it is grown around the world, both as a food ...",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-10-30T16:52:00.0000000Z",
                        "primaryImageOfPage": {
                            "thumbnailUrl": "https://www.bing.com/th?id=OIP.cfNs5TgvS2z-qFGMUr-PLgHaLE&w=80&h=80&c=1&pid=5.1",
                            "width": 80,
                            "height": 80,
                            "sourceWidth": 474,
                            "sourceHeight": 708,
                            "imageId": "OIP.cfNs5TgvS2z-qFGMUr-PLgHaLE"
                        },
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Ornamental+Purslane+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4553378431762717&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=wgBkylR7MN0Wo0WKJ-0RqqzVtrMumRV1",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "The National Gardening Association"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.4",
                        "name": "Purslane - Penn State Extension",
                        "url": "https://extension.psu.edu/purslane",
                        "datePublished": "2022-12-12T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Dec 12, 2022",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://extension.psu.edu/purslane",
                        "snippet": "Purslane can be found in landscape beds, newly seeded or thin turf areas, or cracks in pavement. It has a taproot so hand removal does require some digging. The proper use of mulch in ornamental plant areas can also effectively reduce this weed. There are a number of pre-emergent and post-emergent herbicides labeled for purslane.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T06:53:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Ornamental+Purslane+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4645840487253319&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=mHpqcoeAFq1Ar2x4yd2ecUDeoZdDN6kz",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Penn State Extension"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.5",
                        "name": "What Is Rock Purslane \u2013 Learn About Rock Purslane Growing And Care ...",
                        "url": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/flowers/rock-purslane/rock-purslane-care.htm",
                        "thumbnailUrl": "https://www.bing.com/th?id=OIP.HLO5WEMdxm9pvjOuif_eYwHaE8&w=80&h=80&c=1&pid=5.1",
                        "datePublished": "2021-03-09T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Mar 9, 2021",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/flowers/rock-purslane/rock-purslane-care.htm",
                        "snippet": "Rock purslane plants are suitable for growing in USDA plant hardiness zones 8 and above. They can withstand temps as low as 25 degrees F. (-4 C.) and tolerate drought like a champ. In cooler climates, you can plant rock purslane as an annual. This versatile, spreading plant works well in rock gardens and is an ideal plant for xeriscaping.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-10-27T06:07:00.0000000Z",
                        "primaryImageOfPage": {
                            "thumbnailUrl": "https://www.bing.com/th?id=OIP.HLO5WEMdxm9pvjOuif_eYwHaE8&w=80&h=80&c=1&pid=5.1",
                            "width": 80,
                            "height": 80,
                            "sourceWidth": 474,
                            "sourceHeight": 316,
                            "imageId": "OIP.HLO5WEMdxm9pvjOuif_eYwHaE8"
                        },
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Ornamental+Purslane+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4539501391512164&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=vSIrlC5WQLgQU9aUHKGJv18-z-alYOAi",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Gardening Know How"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.6",
                        "name": "Complete Guide to Purslane Care - Plantglossary",
                        "url": "https://plantglossary.com/purslane/",
                        "thumbnailUrl": "https://www.bing.com/th?id=OIP.ksGBsphrufLbsDmbmQGA9QHaFj&w=80&h=80&c=1&pid=5.1",
                        "datePublished": "2024-06-11T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Jun 11, 2024",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://plantglossary.com/purslane",
                        "snippet": "When it comes to humidity, purslane exhibits resilience. Relative humidity levels under 90% suit the plant, allowing it to grow without issues. This makes it easy for you to care for purslane in a range of environments. Avoid overwatering, as the purslane\u2019s water needs are minimal. It also tolerates moderate salinity, adding to its hardiness.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-04T05:53:00.0000000Z",
                        "primaryImageOfPage": {
                            "thumbnailUrl": "https://www.bing.com/th?id=OIP.ksGBsphrufLbsDmbmQGA9QHaFj&w=80&h=80&c=1&pid=5.1",
