                        "displayUrl": "https://thesurvivalgardener.com/purslane-identification-uses-plant-profile",
                        "snippet": "Purslane Identification and Uses. Common Name(s): Purslane Latin Name: Portulaca oleracea Plant Family: Portulacaceae Size: 6-16\u201d Edible: Yes Medicinal: Yes Where Found: Disturbed ground, open spaces, compacted soil, sandy soil, roadsides, gardens Flowering Time: Year-round, according to rainfall Fruit: Seed pods, appearing after blooms Native: No Uses: Leaves edible raw or cooked",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-10-30T09:52:00.0000000Z",
                        "primaryImageOfPage": {
