                        "displayUrl": "https://americanpeonysociety.org/learn/itoh-peonies",
                        "snippet": "Crown division, the traditional method of propagating all, but the woody peony types, works well with the Itoh Group sorts. During a propagation cycle (3 to 4 years), the underground stem (crown) extends somewhat with tuberous growth and swells with food storage similar in habit to the Lactiflora parent type, facilitating the process of division.",
