                        "snippet": "Noteworthy Characteristics. Ruellia humilis, commonly called wild petunia, is a Missouri native perennial which occurs in dryish soils in open woods, glades, prairies and fields throughout the State except for the far southeastern lowlands.Typically grows to 2' tall. Features tubular, bell-shaped, petunia-like flowers (to 3\" long), each with five shallow rounded lobes.",
