                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningchannel.com/growing-celosia-cockscomb-flowers",
                        "snippet": "A crested type, Celosia cristata, also known as cockscomb celosia. The flower heads resemble the structures of a brain and in some varieties a rooster\u2019s comb. Hence the name. It blooms in red, yellow, pink, white, and orange. A plume type, Celosia argentea, also known as plumed celosia. The flowers appear as feathery plumes and come in the ...",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-05T10:07:00.0000000Z",
