                        "displayUrl": "https://garden.org/plants/view/71542/Cockscomb-Celosia-argentea",
                        "snippet": "Needs specific temperature: 68\u00baF - 75\u00baF. Days to germinate: 7 to 21 days. Depth to plant seed: Shallowly sow at depth of approximately 1/8 inch, covering with a thin layer of soil. Sow in situ. Containers: Suitable in 3 gallon or larger. Needs excellent drainage in pots. Common names. Cockscomb.",
