                        "displayUrl": "https://www.bioexplorer.net/plants/flowers/gayfeather",
                        "snippet": "Gayfeather (Liatris spicata), commonly known as the Blazing Star, Marsh Blazing Star, or Dense Blazing Star, is a tall, erect, lumpy perennial native to low-lying wetlands, grasslands, and marsh edges. It has terminal ends (6 to 12\" long) of stalkless, round, downy, dark purple buds (up to 3/4\" wide each) that appear on stiff, upright, leafy pedicels.",
