                        "displayUrl": "https://plants.usda.gov/DocumentLibrary/plantguide/pdf/pg_ecpu.pdf",
                        "snippet": "1992). The Choctaw use purple coneflower as a cough medicine and gastro-intestinal aid (Moerman 1986). The Delaware used an infusion of coneflower root for gonorrhea and found it to be highly effective. The purple coneflower was the only native prairie plant popularized as a medicine by folk practitioners and doctors.",
