                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.12",
                        "name": "Torch Lilies, Tritomas and Red Hot Pokers, How to Grow a Kniphofia ...",
                        "url": "https://www.thegardenhelper.com/tritoma.html",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.thegardenhelper.com/tritoma.html",
                        "snippet": "An easy to understand guide to growing and caring for Torch Lilies, also known as Tritomas or Red Hot Pokers, with listings of different varieties, watering and light needs and helpful growing tips. The Garden Helper ... Kniphofia uvaria is commonly known as a Red Hot Poker, Torch Lily or sometimes a Tritoma Depending on the variety, the flame ...",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-10-28T14:01:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Red-hot+Poker+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4759876162093125&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=8kZM5PgwT_l0ipEWaX4KlpmKwGp5OlX_",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "The Garden Helper"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.13",
                        "name": "Red Hot Poker Plant Guide: How to Grow & Care for \u201cKniphofia\u201d",
                        "url": "https://gardenbeast.com/red-hot-poker-guide/",
                        "datePublished": "2022-03-10T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Mar 10, 2022",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://gardenbeast.com/red-hot-poker-guide",
                        "snippet": "Sowing Rate: 3 - 4 seeds per plant. Start Red Hot Poker Seed indoors 6 \u2013 8 weeks before the end of frost season. Cover the seed lightly with peat moss and keep them moist. With a temperature range of 70 \u2013 75F, germination is usually in 28 days. Space the plants 18 \u2013 24 inches apart. Grow Red Hot Poker in full sun and in well-drained soil.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T04:37:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Red-hot+Poker+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4584886311125007&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=ZE6dxhfZKhok9wKFhv2vazFMmRI2m20-",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "GardenBeast"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.14",
                        "name": "Red Hot Poker: How To Grow & Care For Torch Lilies - Blooming Backyard",
                        "url": "https://www.bloomingbackyard.com/red-hot-poker/",
                        "datePublished": "2022-03-16T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Mar 16, 2022",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.bloomingbackyard.com/red-hot-poker",
                        "snippet": "Red Hot Poker Diseases and Common Pests. Red Hot Poker is generally disease- and pest-free. Particularly when grown in well-draining soil in full sun in zones 5 to 9. Slugs and snails in abundance may be an issue for these plants. If soil is poorly draining, Red Hot Poker is susceptible to root rot.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T19:13:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Red-hot+Poker+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4788837128929527&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=LdHrGJDulEqBtkXcbsrJ7A6XC7SqWTlI",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Blooming Backyard"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.15",
                        "name": "Planting Red Hot Pokers - How To Care For A Red Hot Poker Plant ...",
                        "url": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/bulbs/red-hot-poker/growing-red-hot-torch-lilies.htm",
                        "datePublished": "2021-06-19T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Jun 19, 2021",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/bulbs/red-hot-poker/growing-red-hot-torch...",
                        "snippet": "What is a Red Hot Poker Torch Lily? The striking, red hot poker plant (Kniphofia uvaria) is in the Liliaceae family and is also known as poker plant and torch lily. This plant thrives in USDA zones 5 through 9 and is an upright evergreen perennial with a clumping habit. Over 70 known species exist of this South African native plant.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T16:05:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Red-hot+Poker+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4625546766713329&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=l8-N218z-0A3dOCHPO_pDjTtR9zhhuzW",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Gardening Know How"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.16",
                        "name": "Red Hot Poker \u2018Glowstick\u2019 - HCMGA",
                        "url": "https://txmg.org/hendersonmg/plant-library/red-hot-poker-glowstick/",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://txmg.org/hendersonmg/plant-library/red-hot-poker-glowstick",
                        "snippet": "Kniphofia uvaria, commonly known as red-hot poker or torch lily, is an upright, clump-forming, rhizomatous perennial that is native to South Africa. Red Hot Poker \u2018Glowstick\u2019 is a new improvement to an old garden favorite. Glowstick flowers its first year with bottlebrush spikes of bright yellow tones. Good for smaller gardens.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-04T23:44:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Red-hot+Poker+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4929952572375155&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=tC40RoBSTbXB4hKrLR05qgaJYuX3l4LX",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Texas Master Gardeners"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.17",
                        "name": "How to Grow Red Hot Poker - American Meadows",
                        "url": "https://www.americanmeadows.com/content/perennials/unique-perennials/how-to-grow-red-hot-poker",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.americanmeadows.com/.../perennials/unique-perennials/how-to-grow-red-hot-poker",
                        "snippet": "Watering: Although established red hot poker plants can withstand dry periods in summer, lack of adequate watering will cause the flowering to be decreased. Provide red hot poker plants with 1 inch of water every week during hot summers. Make sure the water saturates the soil 5 to 6 inches deep each time, but let the soil dry out between waterings.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-01T10:12:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Red-hot+Poker+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=5060811638833375&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=POpB3RXD0kb9ZCTGBsrM7b8XH-dbgIzy",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "American Meadows"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.18",
                        "name": "Pyromania\u00ae 'Backdraft' - Red Hot Poker - Proven Winners",
                        "url": "https://www.provenwinners.com/plants/kniphofia/pyromania-backdraft-red-hot-poker-kniphofia-hybrid",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.provenwinners.com/plants/kniphofia/pyromania-backdraft-red-hot-poker...",
                        "snippet": "I tried 4 of these Pyromania\u2122 'Backdraft' - Red Hot Poker plants last year, and now I'm hooked! They were hardy bloomers in different light conditions (seemed to have equal blooms in Part Sun vs. Full Sun - they are not fussy), produced gorgeous & durable flowering stems ('pokers') virtually all growing season, and were my best garden purchase last season.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T00:56:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Red-hot+Poker+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4862878073029190&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=1O7gMo0HPAijYatpXANXI2O-mzgD79ar",
