                        "snippet": "Silene coronaria, the rose campion, is a species of flowering plant in the family Caryophyllaceae, native to Eurasia. Other common names include dusty miller (which also refers to Centaurea cineraria and Jacobaea maritima), mullein-pink and bloody William.In the United Kingdom it is still widely referenced under its synonym Lychnis coronaria. [1]",
