                        "displayUrl": "https://plantcaretoday.com/rose-campion.html",
                        "snippet": "Rose campion is a perennial but doesn\u2019t last for many years. Most people grow it as a biennial or annual. Rose Campion Flower and Fragrance. The plant blooms in late spring and early summer, with different varieties producing different flowers. Rose campion produces magenta, rose, or reddish flowers with soft, round petals and white flowers.",
