                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardenersworld.com/how-to/grow-plants/rose-campion",
                        "snippet": "Plant rose campion in spring, or in early autumn so it establishes well before the cold, wet weather arrives. Dig a hole no deeper than the rootball of the plant but slightly wider. There's no need to fertilise the planting hole as rose campion thrives in poor soils. Firm gently around the plant and water well. Continue watering until established.",
