                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://myfolia.com/plants/1313-rose-campion-lychnis-coronaria",
                        "snippet": "Growing Rose campion from seed. Easy germination. Start indoors 6-8 weeks prior to last spring frost. Sow seed in container on good seed starting mix. Cover seeds lightly. Moisten mix. Place container in a location at 68-70\u00b0F. Germination should begin in 3-7 days. Easily self seeds.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-10-27T23:28:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Rose+Campion+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=5048004044391085&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=_TzTxUabcuT3kW_8x0oUpDgGUOb3dCwL",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.19",
                        "name": "How to Grow Lychnis - Rose Campion - Harvest to Table",
                        "url": "https://harvesttotable.com/how-to-grow-lychnis/",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://harvesttotable.com/how-to-grow-lychnis",
                        "snippet": "Lychnis propagation. Lychnis and be grown from seed or propagated by division. Lychnis seeds will germinate in 20 to 25 days at 70\u00b0F (21\u00b0C). Seeds sown in autumn or early spring will generally flower in their second year. Divide Lychnis every 2 to 3 years in spring to keep the clump vigorous and for propagation.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T07:15:00.0000000Z",
