                        "snippet": "Portulaca grandiflora is a succulent flowering plant in the purslane family, native to southern Brazil, Argentina, and Uruguay. It has many common names, such as rose moss, moss rose, and sun rose, and is widely grown as an ornamental plant for its bright flowers.",
