                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://gardenerspath.com/plants/flowers/grow-portulaca",
                        "snippet": "Grown as an ornamental annual in temperate areas, moss rose is hardy only in USDA Zones 10 to 12. Most seeds are sold in packets as colorful blends and mixes in single or double flowering forms. And unlike other Portulaca species, such as P. oleracea and P. umbraticola, moss rose is not considered edible because of its bitter taste.",
