                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Sep 15, 2023",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/flowers/russian-sage-flowers/russian-sage...",
                        "snippet": "Pruning Russian Sage. Pruning Russian sage can help you manage the size and encourage bushier growth, but winter pruning is optional. While allowing the stems and seed pods to remain in the garden until spring creates winter interest, if you prefer a tidier appearance, you can cut the stems back to 8 to 12 inches (20 - 30 cm) above the ground.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-01T21:16:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Russian+Sage+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4629042869043248&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=vGQNjtRtZ7c5C433XlJGRoV4VIGM9q-f",
