                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://pnwplants.wsu.edu/PlantDisplay.aspx?PlantID=19",
                        "snippet": "Russian sage is considered a semi-woody groundcover bearing upright, grayish white stems and lobed, silvery gray leaves 1\" wide by 2\" long. Adaptation: This sage does well as either a single specimen plant or in a group with others. It can tolerate a wide array of soil types. For use in a mixed perennial border in the middle to back of the border.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T01:13:00.0000000Z",
