                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.1",
                        "name": "How To Grow Eryngiums (Sea Holly) - BBC Gardeners World Magazine",
                        "url": "https://www.gardenersworld.com/how-to/grow-plants/how-to-grow-eryngiums/",
                        "thumbnailUrl": "https://www.bing.com/th?id=OIP.TUG1RbX4bJSaj2irZGVkUgHaE8&w=80&h=80&c=1&pid=5.1",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardenersworld.com/how-to/grow-plants/how-to-grow-eryngiums",
                        "snippet": "Sea hollies (Eryngium) have spiky leaves and thistle-like flowers in colours ranging from grey to intense cobalt blue, surrounded by a characteristic 'ruff'.They make striking garden plants and have excellent wildlife value, particularly for pollinators. There are over 250 species of Eryngium, including plenty of cultivated varieties. As their name suggests, they grow well in coastal areas.",
