                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eryngium_amethystinum",
                        "snippet": "Eryngium amethystinum, the amethyst eryngo, [1] Italian eryngo [2] or amethyst sea holly, is a clump-forming, perennial, tap-rooted herb.Its stem is 30 to 50 cm long and is light blue to purple in colour. It has a basal circle of obovate, pinnate, spiny, leathery, mid-green leaves.It flowers in mid to late summer with cylindrical umbels, 2\u20133 cm long atop silvery blue bracts and branching stems.",
