                        "snippet": "The Shasta Daisy (Leucantheum x superbum) is a beloved perennial that has captured gardeners\u2019 hearts since the early 20th century.Known for its long-lasting blooms, this plant features cheerful white flowers with bright yellow centers. Blooming during the spring and summer, Shasta daisies bring purity, simplicity, and innocence to your garden.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-10-30T03:29:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Shasta+Daisy+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=1911477123049&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=4Bm1XnvDmQdv-WYU7o7FqrqCosOrsNzE",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.7",
                        "name": "Shasta Daisy Guide: How to Grow and Care for ... - GardenBeast",
                        "url": "https://gardenbeast.com/shasta-daisy-guide/",
                        "thumbnailUrl": "https://www.bing.com/th?id=OIP.YmIdypjMVteb6rdPIudV1AHaE8&w=80&h=80&c=1&pid=5.1",
                        "datePublished": "2022-03-17T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Mar 17, 2022",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://gardenbeast.com/shasta-daisy-guide",
                        "snippet": "Pruning and Deadheading. When the flowers start to fade, gardeners can deadhead the spent blooms to extend the flowering season. After the first frost, cut back the flowering stem to the base of the plant, around an inch above the soil line. The Shasta daisy has excellent heat and cold tolerance in their growing zones.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-01T01:46:00.0000000Z",
                        "primaryImageOfPage": {
