                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/leucanthemum-x-superbum",
                        "snippet": "Phonetic Spelling. lew-KAN-theh-mum soo-PER-bum. Description. Shasta daisies are old-fashioned favorites for perennial borders and cut flowers, with single and double-flowered cultivars available. Plant in average to dry well-drained garden soil in full sun to partial shade. Use in the perennial border, containers, cutting garden or cottage garden.",
