                        "datePublished": "2023-04-07T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Apr 7, 2023",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://gardenerspath.com/plants/flowers/grow-shasta-daisy",
                        "snippet": "Developed near snowy Mount Shasta in Northern California, Shasta daisies are the result of a quadruple hybrid cross. The parents, L. vulgare (oxeye daisy), L. maximum (English field daisy), L. lacustre (Portuguese field daisy), and Nipponanthemum nipponicum (Japanese field daisy) were crossed over a period of 17 years by horticulturalist Luther Burbank, starting in 1884.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-03T22:38:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Shasta+Daisy+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4900184161845585&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=YXiXV_BUoSW0WOWZ9xT16GmrTufPSXRi",
