                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://heirloomroses.com/blogs/perennial-plant-care/shasta-daisy",
                        "snippet": "Shasta Daisy is a much loved perennial that is a cross of a European and Japanese daisy variety and was first introduced in the 1890s. This hardy plant can survive winters down to zone 4 and establishes drought tolerance quickly in the first year of growth. These beautiful blooms are deer and rabbit resistant and will bloom from summer to fall making them a great choice for cutting gardens ...",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-10-30T10:47:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Shasta+Daisy+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4590839137698313&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=rIS8qIJ_CJ8nrF-jvwbdFr8Uor5hqr-1",
