                        "name": "Leucanthemum \u00d7 superbum 'Crazy Daisy' - Plant Finder",
                        "url": "https://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?taxonid=256042",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?taxonid=256042",
                        "snippet": "The hybrid name superbum means superb. \u2018Crazy Daisy\u2019 is a Shasta daisy cultivar that typically grows 2-2.5\u2019 tall. It is noted for its large double blooms (2.5\u201d diameter) with frilly, twisted white rays and yellow center disks. Multiple flowers per stem. Coarsely-toothed, lance-shaped, medium green leaves (basal leaves to 12\u201d long).",
