                        "snippet": "With clean, sharp pruners or a knife, cut a 4- to 6-inch piece from a healthy stem. Remove the bottom leaves. Insert the cutting in a 4-inch pot filled with soilless potting mix. Water it well and keep it evenly moist. After a few weeks, you should see new growth, which indicates that the plant is rooting.",
