                            "hostPageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4b/Sedum_spectabile_-_blossom_top_%28aka%29.jpg",
                            "width": 110,
                            "height": 110,
                            "sourceWidth": 2476,
                            "sourceHeight": 2000
                        },
                        "description": "Hylotelephium spectabile is a species of flowering plant in the stonecrop family Crassulaceae, native to China and Korea. Its common names include showy stonecrop, iceplant, and butterfly stonecrop. Growing to 45 cm tall and broad, it is an herbaceous perennial with alternate, simple, toothed leaves on erect, unbranched succulent stems and has a tuber root rhizome. The leaves are usually arranged opposite or in threes, simple and more or less wedge-shaped at the base, and frosted blue above; they are 2.5 to 10 cm long and 0.8 to 5 cm wide. The leaf margin is smooth or serrated towards the tip. Stipules are missing.",
