                        "displayUrl": "https://countryhomeandblooms.com/siberian-iris",
                        "snippet": "One of the reasons the Siberian iris is so popular with gardeners is its hardiness, in USDA zones 3-9. This plant can survive in a wide range of growing conditions, from full sun to partial shade, and can tolerate a range of soil types, from sandy to clay. Siberian irises prefer moist soil, but are drought-tolerant once established.",
