                        "snippet": "Low maintenance, requiring only feeding and division every few years. Ideal for ponds, streams, or boggy areas. In beds, Siberian iris requires a few extra waterings in a season. Propagation Lift and divide clumps, or separate bulb offsets, and plant immediately in early autumn. Problems Iris borer, verbena bud moth, whiteflies, iris weevil ...",
