                        "snippet": "Siberian iris plants. Siberian iris is a hardy, long-lived type of beardless iris consisting of clumps of narrow, sword-like leaves and slender stems that reach heights up to 4 feet (1 m.). The graceful, grass-like leaves remain attractive long after the flowers have faded.",
