                        "snippet": "Hosta sieboldiana is a large hosta native to Japan. It is a clump-forming perennial that typically matures in a spreading foliage mound to 24\" tall and to 48-60\" wide. Thick, puckered, cupped, wide-oval, green leaves (to 14\u201d long and 12\u201d wide) have distinctive veining, cuspidate tips and cordate lobes. Leaves often emerge smoky-blue in spring.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-03T14:51:00.0000000Z",
