                        "snippet": "Hosta Species Update The Hosta Library ORG20070416 \u00a9W. George Schmid 2007 Original Issue ORG2007.04.16 Revised Issue REV 2/2010.08.27 H. longissima Honda J. Japanese Botany, 13:894 1937 and Maekawa J. of the Faculty of Science, Imperial University Tokyo, Section 3 Botany, Vol. 5:404 1940",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-04T04:37:00.0000000Z",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": true,
                        "siteName": "Hosta Library"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.13",
                        "name": "Hosta sieboldiana 'Frances Williams' - Plant Finder",
                        "url": "https://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?taxonid=248945",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?taxonid=248945",
                        "snippet": "Hosta sieboldiana is a large hosta native to Japan. It is a clump-forming perennial that typically matures in a spreading foliage mound to 24\" tall and to 48-60\" wide. Thick, puckered, cupped, wide-oval, green leaves (to 14\u201d long and 12\u201d wide) have distinctive veining, cuspidate tips and cordate lobes. Leaves often emerge smoky-blue in spring.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-01T12:11:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Siebold+Hosta+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4596989526737114&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=9HKF7f4tQg0qeDJfmOQ8vT41MrF6Vqh3",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Missouri Botanical Garden"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.14",
                        "name": "H. sieboldiana \u30c8\u30ae\u30dc\u30a6\u30b7 Part 1 - HOSTA LIBRARY",
                        "url": "https://www.hostalibrary.org/species/pdf/sieboldiana1.pdf",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.hostalibrary.org/species/pdf/sieboldiana1.pdf",
                        "snippet": "This hosta has received a detailed histo-ry in this Species Update because it is the pod parent of H. sieboldiana \u2018Elegans\u2019 (= H. \u2018Elegans\u2019), which poses as the species H. sieboldiana in horticul-ture the world over. As pointed out on page 2, H. \u2018Elegans\u2019 is of hybrid origin, thus: H. fortunei (= H. \u2018Tokudama\u2019) \u00d7.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T18:42:00.0000000Z",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": true,
                        "siteName": "Hosta Library"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.15",
                        "name": "Hosta sieboldii 'Kabitan' - Plant Finder - Missouri Botanical Garden",
                        "url": "https://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?kempercode=p500",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?kempercode=...",
                        "snippet": "Noteworthy Characteristics. Hosta sieboldii 'Kabitan' features a mound of ruffled, narrow, variegated leaves with gold centers and green edges with racemes of dark lavender flowers on 20\" scapes. A dependable and versatile perennial requiring little care. Grown primarily for its beautiful foliage which provides color, contrast and texture to the landscape.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-05T17:18:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Siebold+Hosta+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4955168326156323&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=lzud3zzIUCrNWYlTcQxxgCxaLcey236S",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Missouri Botanical Garden"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.16",
                        "name": "Hosta Species Update The Hosta Library ORG20070316 \u00a9W",
                        "url": "https://www.hostalibrary.org/species/pdf/sieboldii3.pdf",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.hostalibrary.org/species/pdf/sieboldii3.pdf",
                        "snippet": "Introduction: The maternal inheritance of plastogene mutants in Hosta was first demonstrated by Yasui (1929) and later corroborated by Vaughn (1980). Vaughn\u2019s study included a number of H. sieboldii mutants and demonstrated that the occur-rence of plastogene mutations is frequent in this species complex.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-03T15:28:00.0000000Z",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": true,
                        "siteName": "Hosta Library"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.17",
                        "name": "Hosta sieboldiana - Plant Finder - Missouri Botanical Garden",
