                        "snippet": "Viburnum sieboldii, commonly called Siebold viburnum, is an upright, rounded, multi-stemmed, deciduous shrub or small tree that typically grows to 15-20\u2019 tall and to 10-15' wide. It is native to Japan. Opposite, toothed, elliptic to oblong, medium to dark green leaves (to 3\u201d long) usually develop no appreciable fall color.",
