                        "displayUrl": "https://gobotany.nativeplanttrust.org/species/cotinus/coggygria",
                        "snippet": "Facts. European smoketree is widely cultivated as a care- free shrub in North America; this species originally comes from Europe and China. Its common name refers to its panicles of tiny greenish-yellow flowers, which \"explode\" into bloom in June, the inflorescences gradually drying to puffy clusters resembling plumes of smoke.",
