                        "snippet": "Cotinus obovatus, American Smoketree, is sometimes inaccurately described as having large, showy pink flowers. In fact, Smoketree gets its common name from the billowy hairs attached to elongated stalks on the spent flower clusters. These hairs turn a smoky-pink to purplish-pink in summer, covering the tree with fluffy, hazy, smoke-like puffs.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-10-29T06:18:00.0000000Z",
