                        "snippet": "A relatively large shrub, spicebush reaches heights of 6 to 12 feet (2-4 m.) at maturity, with a similar spread. The shrub is valued not only for its scent, but for the emerald green leaves which, with enough sunlight, turn a lovely shade of yellow in autumn. Spicebush is dioecious, which means that male and female flowers are on separate plants.",
