                        "displayUrl": "https://www.canr.msu.edu/nativeplants/uploads/files/Northern_spicebush.pdf",
                        "snippet": "Plant forms oval green berries that ripen to bright red in September. Plants grow 1-4 feet tall. Leaves of this species have a distinct spicy scent when rubbed. Habitat quality: This species is native but not sun-tolerant and not part of prairie fen systems. It is a species likely to be on upland edges under invasive shrubs such as buckthorn.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T12:37:00.0000000Z",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": true,
                        "siteName": "College of Agriculture & Natural Resources"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.17",
                        "name": "Spicebush - Ohio Department of Natural Resources",
                        "url": "https://ohiodnr.gov/discover-and-learn/plants-trees/broad-leaf-trees/Spicebush-Lindera-benzoin",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://ohiodnr.gov/discover-and-learn/plants-trees/broad-leaf-trees/Spicebush-Lindera...",
                        "snippet": "Spicebush. Spicebush (Lindera benzoin), found throughout all of Ohio, is usually found as an understory shrub of moist to wet woodlands that is one of the first shrubs to bloom, usually in late winter. Its twigs and branchlets, when scraped, emit a spicy fragrance. Bright red fruits appear in late summer and early autumn on female shrubs and ...",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T15:29:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Spice+bush+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4922221636026811&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=xQf3j7bZ5Li-Xl_RYh8Y_8p73lESaDH9",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Ohio Department of Health"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.18",
                        "name": "Spicebush, Common - Wildfoods 4 Wildlife",
                        "url": "https://wildfoods4wildlife.com/monographs/common-spicebush/",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://wildfoods4wildlife.com/monographs/common-spicebush",
                        "snippet": "Seed/ Fruit Size: The single seeded berry\u2014a drupe \u2014is bright red, oblong and shiny, and when crushed in your fingers smells lemony spicy. Berries average around 1/4 inch (6 mm) wide by 7/16 inch (1 cm) long. This fruit is not very fleshy\u2013the seed is large as in many wild fruits\u2013but is high in fats.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-03T01:38:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Spice+bush+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4541112001429823&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=julMogj9ff0RDziax0qzI2GWItNyketi",
