                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://hort.extension.wisc.edu/articles/spider-flower-cleome-hassleriana",
                        "snippet": "Cleome, or spider flower, in bloom. Cleome is a genus of about 170 species in the caper family (Capparaceae). Spider flower, Cleome hassleriana (sometimes referred to incorrectly as C. hasslerana or by the synonym C. spinosa) is a common annual flower from South America (Paraguay, Uruguay, Argentina and southern Brazil) that also goes by other common names including spider legs and grandfather ...",
                        "deepLinks": [
                            {
                                "name": "Spider plant, Chlorophytum comosum",
                                "url": "https://hort.extension.wisc.edu/articles/spider-plant-chlorophytum-comosum/",
                                "snippet": "Spider plant produces small white flowers. Long, wiry stems up to 2 feet long are produced, sometimes with a few small leaves, especially in response to short days and long, uninterrupted nights for at least three weeks, although they may appear at any time of year indoors. Small white, star-shaped flowers are produced at the ends of the stems."
                            }
