                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://whatsinaname.hmnh.harvard.edu/sugar-maple",
                        "snippet": "The sugar maple is sometimes called \"rock maple\" or the \"hard maple.\" The \u201csugar\u201d common name, is a tribute to the tree\u2019s sweet, delicious maple syrup product. Sugar maples can reach up to 100 feet in height and collectively grow on around 31 million acres of land. Climate change threatens to impact sugar maples, which depend on ...",
