                        "snippet": "Too much sun causes the variegation to fade or turn solid green. Blue hosta varieties get their signature color from a waxy coating on the leaves This coating melts away in very sunny, hot conditions. Hostas native to Asian woodlands and forests evolved for filtered light conditions. Their DNA is designed for shade tolerance.",
