                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://milnepublishing.geneseo.edu/botany/chapter/sunflower",
                        "snippet": "Phylogeny. Helianthus is a genus in the sunflower family (Asteraceae), one of the largest families angiosperms. There are roughly 70 species, both annual and perennial, with H. annuus (an annual) being the most important crop species. A perennial species (H. tuberosus), called Jerusalem artichoke, is occasionally grown for its edible tubers.",
