                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.britannica.com/plant/common-sunflower",
                        "snippet": "The common sunflower (H. annuus) is an annual herb with a rough hairy stem 1\u20134.5 metres (3\u201315 feet) high and broad, coarsely toothed, rough leaves 7.5\u201330 cm (3\u201312 inches) long arranged in spirals. The attractive heads of flowers are 7.5\u201315 cm wide in wild specimens and\u2026. Read More.",
