                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://kids.britannica.com/kids/article/sunflower/353826",
                        "snippet": "Sunflowers are giants among flowers. The rough, hairy stem grows from 3 to 15 feet (1 to 4.5 meters) tall. The leaves are wide, rough, and 3 to 12 inches (8 to 30 centimeters) long. The bloom of a sunflower has two parts. The center is a disk of small flowers packed closely together. The disk flowers are brown, yellow, or purple.",
