                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://plants.usda.gov/DocumentLibrary/plantguide/pdf/pg_hean3.pdf",
                        "snippet": "General: Sunflower Family (Asteraceae). The sunflower is an erect, coarse, tap-rooted annual with rough-hairy stems 6-30 dm (2-10 ft) tall. The leaves are mostly alternate, egg-shaped to triangular, and entire or toothed. The flower heads are 7.5-15 cm (3-6 in) wide and at the ends of branches.",
