                        "displayUrl": "https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/.../common-name/variegated-solomons-seal",
                        "snippet": "Solomon's Seal is typically used as a shade-loving foliage plant and combines well with Hostas, Astilbes, and Bleeding Hearts. Its variegated leaves and small white bell-shaped flowers brighten and add variety to a shade garden. It can be slow to establish in the garden but is long lived and low maintenance.",
