                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://garden.org/plants/view/78465/Variegated-Solomons-Seal-Polygonatum-odoratum-var...",
                        "snippet": "Variegated Solomon's Seal is a nice choice for shady areas. Its taller, arched stems add a nice form and texture to the shade bed. It makes a nice background plant behind hostas. It spreads, but not invasively, so that each spring I can divide and move some to another area or share with friends. Its flowers are small and last a short time, so I ...",
