                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.11",
                        "name": "Solomon's Seal Growing: How To Plant Solomon's Seal - Gardening Know How",
                        "url": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/foliage/solomons-seal/caring-for-solomons-seal.htm",
                        "datePublished": "2021-07-26T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Jul 26, 2021",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/foliage/solomons-seal/caring-for-solomons...",
                        "snippet": "False Solomon's seal has similar, opposite leaves, but flowers on the end of the stem in a cluster. False Solomon's seal growing info says the berries of this plant are a ruby red color. The green leaved specimen and False Solomon's seal are native to the United States, while variegated types are native to Europe, Asia, and the United States.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-01T22:28:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Variegated+Solomon%27s+Seal+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4567057903649136&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=yzCTh8FfyG8c29w3PmJEg8o8pXqJ302z",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Gardening Know How"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.12",
                        "name": "How to Grow and Use Solomon's Seal - Dengarden",
                        "url": "https://dengarden.com/Solomons-Seal",
                        "datePublished": "2018-09-13T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Sep 13, 2018",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://dengarden.com/Solomons-Seal",
                        "snippet": "Here are three particular varieties to try in your garden (as suggested by The Spruce): True Solomon\u2019s Seal (P. biflorum): Very dependable and one of the fastest growing varieties.; Fragrant Solomon's Seal (P. odoratum \"Variegatum\"): Variegated form with white tips.; Fragrant Solomon's Seal (Polygonatum. biflorum var. commutatum): Grows to about five feet in height.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T12:17:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Variegated+Solomon%27s+Seal+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=330879746298&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=QI4PFOhLJ6J0A7PekXpTt3xY8f45NfKm",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Dengarden"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.13",
                        "name": "How to Grow and Care for Solomon's Seal",
                        "url": "https://growhappierplants.com/solomons-seal/",
                        "datePublished": "2023-01-30T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Jan 30, 2023",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://growhappierplants.com/solomons-seal",
                        "snippet": "Where to Plant Solomon's Seal. Solomon's seal needs a shady location to grow, so choose a site with partial to full shade, such as the north side of a house or under dense tree canopies. A bit of sunlight in the morning is okay but avoid afternoon sun exposure. Once the plants get established, they easily tolerate mild drought conditions.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-03T03:15:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Variegated+Solomon%27s+Seal+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4821302789734686&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=2VE9_vHJS1KQebS92EAt26MGdV5y4QdZ",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.14",
                        "name": "Giant Solomon's Seal: A Plant Fit For A King - Dave's Garden",
                        "url": "https://davesgarden.com/guides/articles/view/3697/",
                        "datePublished": "2012-04-10T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Apr 10, 2012",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://davesgarden.com/guides/articles/view/3697",
                        "snippet": "If you don\u2019t have room for the giant variety, consider planting the lovely variegated Solomon's Seal (P. odoratum var. pluriflorum 'Variegatum') , or pair the two. The variegated Solomon\u2019s seal is a much more delicate plant, reaching a height of 2 to 3 feet with a spread of 1 foot or under.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T02:19:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Variegated+Solomon%27s+Seal+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4833453251363460&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=xITmL98d9t-WAHHET48N5EzaoBz-7NTu",
                        "language": "en",
