                        "snippet": "Most wheat and plume celosias are planted between 9 and 12 inches apart. A well-branched cockscomb variety will need between 12 and 18 inches between plants. In containers, the dwarf plumed varieties can be grown relatively close together, though the dwarf cockscomb varieties may need more spacing due to their wider, brainy flower-heads.",
