                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Dec 10, 2022",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://goldenspikecompany.com/celosia-cockscomb-flowe",
                        "snippet": "Celosia is a genus of tiny bright blooms that grow in clumps. Long-lasting plumes of feathery flowers that grow as colorful spikes characterize some celosia varieties. The cockscomb has twisted plumes that look like a rooster\u2019s comb, hence the name. Other celosia blooms include little spiked wheat-like heads.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-10-24T18:21:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Wheat+Cockscomb+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4950465334084676&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=jaTRdzs5D7HLNmLwnEhn5Zquvx5AEsYp",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Golden Spike Company"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.14",
                        "name": "10 Best Celosia Flower Varieties For Your Garden - Gardening Chores",
                        "url": "https://www.gardeningchores.com/celosia-flower-varieties/",
                        "datePublished": "2022-04-13T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Apr 13, 2022",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningchores.com/celosia-flower-varieties",
                        "snippet": "Botanical name: Celosia spp. Common name(s): cockscomb, mfungu (its Swahili name). Plant type: herbaceous annual or tender perennials, some are perennial shrubs though. Size: it depends on the species, most range from 6 inches to 3 feet tall (15 cm to 90 cm).Some species can reach 13 feet tall (4 meters). Potting soil: peat based or /and compost rich and well drained soil.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T17:02:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Wheat+Cockscomb+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4766271372198533&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=feW0HUibEmh3c26QuQ1vcmWk3fOKXG8L",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Gardening Chores"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.15",
                        "name": "Growing Celosia From Seed | Johnny's Selected Seeds",
                        "url": "https://www.johnnyseeds.com/growers-library/flowers/celosia/celosia-key-growing-information.html",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.johnnyseeds.com/.../flowers/celosia/celosia-key-growing-information.html",
                        "snippet": "SOWING: Transplant (recommended) - Sow into 72-cell flats or preferred seedling container 6-8 weeks before planting out. Light is required for germination; cover very lightly to hold seeds in place. Grow seedlings at 63-68\u00b0F (17-20\u00b0C). Harden off and transplant out after danger of frost. Direct seed - Only in locations with a long growing season.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-03T02:58:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Wheat+Cockscomb+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4631658505240943&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=BrY2QgkY92g6PD-3gfL-zArRfmyNv7Qz",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Johnny's Selected Seeds"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.16",
                        "name": "14 Stunning Types of Celosia You Can Grow - Balcony Garden Web",
                        "url": "https://balconygardenweb.com/stunning-types-of-celosia/",
                        "datePublished": "2024-08-13T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Aug 13, 2024",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://balconygardenweb.com/stunning-types-of-celosia",
                        "snippet": "Types of Celosia. 1. Crested Coxcomb. shutterstock/sarawut muensang. Botanical Name: Celosia cristata. USDA Zone: 9-12. Best Varieties: Celosia Cristata Magenta, Giant red-crested cockscomb, Lemon-lime celocia cristata. This sculptural and decorative celosia variety looks like the crown of a rooster or hen!",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-10-31T13:39:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Wheat+Cockscomb+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4631177467593117&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=SATkTitovmI6BDuEr3O46ZiPOLqUbHaV",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Balcony Garden Web"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.17",
                        "name": "How to Grow Celosia (Cockscomb) Flowers - Gardening Channel",
                        "url": "https://www.gardeningchannel.com/growing-celosia-cockscomb-flowers/",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningchannel.com/growing-celosia-cockscomb-flowers",
                        "snippet": "Apply a 3 to 6-inch layer of soil amendment 10 to 12 inches deep into your garden beds. Add sulfur, should you need to lower the pH and lime should you need to raise it. The plant prefers a pH of 6.0\u20137.0. Although drought-tolerant, water your cockscomb flowers regularly.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-05T10:07:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Wheat+Cockscomb+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4941441613758834&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=e5STbiBo4FHHG8QUSsfuWLp1hs5LNtk4",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "Gardening Channel"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.18",
                        "name": "How to Grow and Care for Cockscomb Flower (Celosia spp.) - GrowingVale",
                        "url": "https://growingvale.com/flowers/cockscomb-care/",
                        "datePublished": "2022-03-01T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Mar 1, 2022",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://growingvale.com/flowers/cockscomb-care",
                        "snippet": "Make a hole large enough to comfortably house the root ball, and gently tease out the cockscomb plant from its container taking care not to break any roots. Place it into the hole at the same depth it was growing in its container, fill in with soil, and firm the soil down around the plant. Water well to settle in.",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T18:57:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Wheat+Cockscomb+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4641566995972472&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=jjc1-vi81n0-vb8fm8TGzKL09u3ObSOg",
                        "language": "en",
                        "isNavigational": false,
                        "noCache": false,
                        "siteName": "GrowingVale"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "https://api.bing.microsoft.com/api/v7/#WebPages.19",
                        "name": "Celosia Care: Learn About Growing Flamingo Cockscomb - Gardening Know How",
                        "url": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/flowers/cockscomb/growing-flamingo-cockscomb.htm",
                        "datePublished": "2021-02-03T00:00:00.0000000",
                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Feb 3, 2021",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningknowhow.com/ornamental/flowers/cockscomb/growing-flamingo...",
                        "snippet": "Caring for Flamingo Cockscomb. Celosia care is relatively simple. Water flamingo cockscomb plants regularly. Although the plant is somewhat drought tolerant, flower spikes are smaller and less dramatic in dry conditions. Keep in mind that the soil should be moist but never waterlogged. Apply a weak solution of a general-purpose, water-soluble ...",
                        "dateLastCrawled": "2024-11-02T15:01:00.0000000Z",
                        "cachedPageUrl": "http://cc.bingj.com/cache.aspx?q=Wheat+Cockscomb+(biology+OR+information+OR+botany+OR+scientific)+-blog+-shopping&d=4717450477764933&mkt=en-US&setlang=en-US&w=kdzcJhkXY55hP8BeAwVVYBfMlS_qcUy2",
