                        "displayUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmos_sulphureus",
                        "snippet": "a Cosmos sp. at Yogyakarta region of Indonesia. Cosmos sulphureus is a species of flowering plant in the sunflower family Asteraceae, also known as sulfur cosmos and yellow cosmos. It is native to Mexico, Central America, and northern South America, and naturalized in other parts of North and South America as well as in Europe, Asia, and Australia.",
