                        "datePublishedDisplayText": "Jan 26, 2022",
                        "isFamilyFriendly": true,
                        "displayUrl": "https://www.gardeningetc.com/advice/types-of-cosmos",
                        "snippet": "What are the best types of cosmos for cut flowers? Cut-flower expert and nursery owner Sarah Raven is a huge fan of using cosmos as cutting garden flowers. 'Cosmos bipinnatus lasts 10 days in the vase, produces two buckets of cut flowers a week from a 3ft (90cm) x 3ft (90cm) patch, and does so from late June until November,' she says.",
